  "bio": [
    "Lin Muqin is the chairman and CEO of energy drink maker Eastroc Beverage (Group), which is dual-listed in Shanghai and Hong Kong.",
    "The mogul started out as a technician at a state-owned construction firm, and later found a job at a Shenzhen-based beverage company.",
    "In 1997 he joined Eastroc, then a state-run beverage business, as its vice president. Lin reportedly scraped together more than 4 million yuan ($570,000) to acquire that firm in early 2000s.",
    "He soon focused on making energy drinks. He managed to build Eastroc into China's largest energy drink maker by sales volume partly through offering products at cheaper prices.",
    "Eastroc has diversified into other market segments including coffee and tea-based beverages."
